      <div class="entry">
        <p>Look how different philosophers are from one another:</p>

<p>Wittgenstein’s last words (upon hearing that friends are coming to visit him): “Tell them I’ve had a wonderful life”</p>

<p>Kierkegaard’s were “My life is a great, to others unknown and incomprehensible suffering.”</p>

<p>Seems that Wittgenstein and Kierkegaard are the modern version of the laughing and the crying philosopher.</p>


